{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:16384554 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:16384554 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"16384554","source":"MED","pmid":"16384554","doi":"10.1016/j.exppara.2005.11.012","title":"Plasmodium falciparum: the fungal metabolite gliotoxin inhibits proteasome proteolytic activity and exerts a plasmodicidal effect on P. falciparum.","authorString":"Hatabu T, Hagiwara M, Taguchi N, Kiyozawa M, Suzuki M, Kano S, Sato K.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Hatabu T","firstName":"Toshimitsu","lastName":"Hatabu","initials":"T","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Gunma University School of Health Sciences, 3-39-15 Showa-machi, Maebashi, Gunma 371-8514, Japan. hatabu@health.gunma-u.ac.jp"}]}},{"fullName":"Hagiwara M","firstName":"Masaki","lastName":"Hagiwara","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Taguchi N","firstName":"Nao","lastName":"Taguchi","initials":"N","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0009-1213-0949"}},{"fullName":"Kiyozawa M","firstName":"Masayuki","lastName":"Kiyozawa","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Suzuki M","firstName":"Mamoru","lastName":"Suzuki","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Kano S","firstName":"Shigeyuki","lastName":"Kano","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Sato K","firstName":"Kumiko","lastName":"Sato","initials":"K"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0009-1213-0949"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"112","journalIssueId":1298651,"dateOfPublication":"2006 Mar","monthOfPublication":3,"yearOfPublication":2006,"printPublicationDate":"2006-03-01","journal":{"title":"Experimental parasitology","medlineAbbreviation":"Exp Parasitol","essn":"1090-2449","issn":"0014-4894","isoabbreviation":"Exp Parasitol","nlmid":"0370713"}},"pubYear":"2006","pageInfo":"179-183","abstractText":"The in vitro antimalarial activity of the fungal metabolite gliotoxin (GTX) was evaluated, and its mechanism of action was studied. GTX showed plasmodicidal activity against both Plasmodium falciparum chloroquine-resistant strain K-1 and chloroquine-susceptible strain FCR-3. GTX cytotoxicity was significantly lower against a normal liver cell line (Chang Liver cells). The intracellular reduced glutathione level of parasitized and of normal red blood cells was not affected by GTX treatment. However, GTX decreased the chymotrypsin-like activity of parasite proteasomes in a time-dependent manner. The results of this study indicate that GTX possesses plasmodicidal activity and that this effect is due to inhibition of parasite proteasome activity, suggesting that GTX may constitute a useful antimalarial therapy.","affiliation":"Gunma University School of Health Sciences, 3-39-15 Showa-machi, Maebashi, Gunma 371-8514, Japan. hatabu@health.gunma-u.ac.jp","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Liver","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"CY","qualifierName":"cytology","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Erythrocytes","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"PS","qualifierName":"parasitology","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Line"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Plasmodium falciparum","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"met